@aataraxiaa to summarize the timer fix:

It turned out that App Settings use `DefaultBrowserPreferences` , and other views mostly use `DefaultBrowserProvider` . I decided to use the latter, as `DefaultBrowserPreferences` also uses it under the hood. 

`DefaultBrowserProvider` shows the default browser prompt when triggered by other models (e.g. `ContinueSetUpModel`) and is a struct dependency, so each model will have its own instance. `VPNUpsellVisibilityManager` doesn’t trigger the dialog howerver, it’s only interested in the results, so I decided to fire a notification when the prompt is shown. As a response to this, `VPNUpsellVisibilityManager` will query the default browser status for a minute (a pattern I’ve seen from other implementations, e.g `DefaultBrowserPreferences`).

