@tomasstrba, "The Open button for suppresed (about:) pop-ups doing nothing looks like a bug":
I mean, if there's a delayed `about:blank` pop-up window blocked, the "Pop-up blocked" window still shows the "Open" button. but when you click the button nothing happens: the Temporary allowance for the following pop-ups would be set, but for the user it looks like a bug – the Open button is clicked, but the pop-up isn't opened.
So my suggestion would be to change the button to "Allow pop-ups" instead of "Open" when an empty pop-up is blocked. Keeping "Open" for non-empty pop-ups that would actually open on click.

